WEBVTT

00:47.189 --> 00:50.193
Okay, Peter, I'm off to my book club.
You'll babysit Stewie?

00:50.360 --> 00:53.488
- Only if I can have a Popsicle.
- Only if you say it right.

00:53.697 --> 00:55.742
"Popsicle. "

00:55.950 --> 00:58.202
Good. And you better be
responsible tonight.

00:58.411 --> 01:02.124
I don't want a repeat of the last time
I left you alone with one of our children.

01:04.376 --> 01:08.006
- It's just so horrible.
- I'm sorry, Lois.

01:08.214 --> 01:12.052
I thought if I shook him enough,
he'd stop crying.

01:12.802 --> 01:14.430
I was kind of right.

01:17.266 --> 01:20.646
Yeah, I'm babysitting for Stewie.
I babysit now, because I'm growing up.

01:20.854 --> 01:25.485
I am so getting hair down there. Anyway,
you guys should totally come over.

01:25.693 --> 01:28.071
What? You're already here? No way.

01:29.948 --> 01:32.993
Look, I brought four cigarettes
I filched from my mom's purse.

01:33.202 --> 01:36.706
Oh, give me one. I wanna look adult.

01:37.332 --> 01:39.125
Hey, watch this.

01:41.252 --> 01:44.090
Oh, yeah? Watch this.

01:45.591 --> 01:47.636
Yeah? Watch this.

01:54.435 --> 01:58.565
- Okay, Quagmire's turn. Truth or dare?
- I pick dare. No, no, no, truth, truth.

01:58.732 --> 02:00.734
Okay, truth. Do you have AIDS?

02:00.984 --> 02:03.862
Aw. Come on, we're all just trying
to have a good time.

02:04.072 --> 02:05.990
Okay, Cleveland, your turn.
Truth or dare?

02:06.199 --> 02:08.034
- Um... Dare.
- Okay.

02:08.243 --> 02:11.330
I dare you to make out with Joe
for 15 seconds.

02:11.539 --> 02:13.416
- What?
- No way. Oh! Oh!

02:13.624 --> 02:16.169
- You gotta, it's a dare. That's the game.
- That's the game.

02:16.378 --> 02:18.713
Okay, what the hell?
I'm an open-minded person.

02:18.922 --> 02:21.426
- So am I. No big deal.
- Just my body.

02:21.634 --> 02:25.054
Oh, my God. They're gonna do it.
Oh, I gotta take a picture.

02:25.263 --> 02:26.974
- Holy crap. No way.
- They're doing it.

02:27.141 --> 02:29.059
No freaking way. Quagmire,
take a picture.

02:29.268 --> 02:31.687
- Oh, God. Oh, my God.
- Oh, my God.

02:33.106 --> 02:37.318
Hey, keep it down.
It's just two guys making out. Relax.

02:37.485 --> 02:40.447
- Stewie, go to bed.
- Am I expected to put myself to bed?

02:40.656 --> 02:42.408
Is no one taking care of me?

02:42.616 --> 02:46.288
Ugh! He's a worse dad than
a rich New York City investment banker.

02:46.496 --> 02:49.416
Hi, Daddy. At school today,
they picked one kid to...

02:49.625 --> 02:52.879
- Millie, it's in here again.
- Me sorry, Mr. Sir.

02:53.087 --> 02:55.424
Get out the room there.
You bother your father.

02:55.632 --> 02:57.968
Him unhappy him had you
in the first place.

02:58.177 --> 03:01.890
Now, come on, I'll let you
rub some lotion on my elbows.

03:02.098 --> 03:04.017
<i>We now return to Robert Mitchum...</i>

03:04.225 --> 03:06.812
<i>...in Out-of-Shape In-Shape Guy
From the '50s.</i>

03:07.855 --> 03:09.857
<i>Gambling is illegal in this town.</i>

03:10.065 --> 03:11.859
<i>- Says who?
- Says me.</i>

03:12.026 --> 03:16.072
<i>- You got a problem with that?
- I'm not really sure.</i>

03:16.281 --> 03:17.657
<i>Kind of waiting for you to exhale.</i>

03:19.827 --> 03:22.496
<i>Actually, yeah,
I do have a problem with that.</i>

03:22.663 --> 03:28.170
Oh, come on. Stupid satellite TV.
Maybe I have to fix the dish.

03:30.798 --> 03:31.799
Uh-oh.

03:33.468 --> 03:37.681
Oh, no. Oh, no. Hey. Hey. Help! Help!

03:40.392 --> 03:43.480
- Hey. Hey, Brian. Brian.
- What the hell?

03:43.647 --> 03:45.899
Call the fire brigade. Get a ladder.
Get me down.

03:46.107 --> 03:48.194
- What are you doing?
- Fucking your girlfriend.

03:48.402 --> 03:51.238
- What do you think? I'm stuck.
- How'd you get on the roof?

03:51.447 --> 03:54.409
Am I doing an interview?
Shut up and get a ladder or something.

03:54.618 --> 03:56.411
Yeah, maybe we are doing an interview.

03:56.578 --> 03:59.165
So tell us about that new project
you have coming up.

03:59.374 --> 04:01.167
What are you talking about?
Get me down.

04:01.376 --> 04:03.336
No. First, tell me about
that new project.

04:03.544 --> 04:06.006
- Oh, you're so dead.
- Is that the title of your new film?

04:06.215 --> 04:10.261
Aah! I've been working on a new movie,
and it's great. Toss me a rope.

04:10.428 --> 04:12.430
No, that's not good enough.
I want details.

04:12.639 --> 04:15.393
I'm gonna slit your throat in your sleep.

04:15.601 --> 04:17.812
Well, when you're working
with Jack Black...

04:18.020 --> 04:19.730
...you just gotta keep up, you know?

04:19.939 --> 04:21.817
I mean, he's doing his thing,
and you gotta...

04:22.025 --> 04:23.860
...match his energy level
without looking...

04:24.069 --> 04:27.407
...like you're trying to one-up him.
That's a game you're not gonna win.

04:27.615 --> 04:32.079
What was it like performing the words
of Oscar-winner Diablo Cody?

04:32.287 --> 04:35.124
She's a goddamn overpriced call girl
who got lucky once.

04:35.332 --> 04:37.752
Ooh. That doesn't sound like
an interview answer.

04:37.961 --> 04:40.046
Say something nice about Diablo Cody.

04:40.255 --> 04:43.258
I envy the tattoo artist...

04:43.426 --> 04:46.679
...who had that huge canvas
of arm fat to work with.

04:46.887 --> 04:48.973
Ha-ha-ha. Wonderful, wonderful.

04:49.182 --> 04:50.976
Hey, listen,
can you hang with us through the break?

04:51.143 --> 04:53.186
- What?
- We'll be back with Stewie's costar...

04:53.395 --> 04:55.064
...Robin Williams.

04:55.273 --> 04:57.150
No, no. I hate Robin Will...
Where are you going?

04:59.569 --> 05:01.613
- Stewie.
- What?

05:01.822 --> 05:04.825
I have to tell you about the future.

05:05.033 --> 05:09.164
- What?
- I have to tell you about the future.

05:09.330 --> 05:12.168
- On the night I go back...
- Wait, wait, wait. No, no, no.

05:12.376 --> 05:16.505
Hang on, Michael.
I have to tell you about your future.

05:16.839 --> 05:18.550
Peter, Stewie's on the roof.

05:18.842 --> 05:21.344
Oh, Nick Jonas is so cute.

05:21.553 --> 05:23.013
- Hey, Peter.
- Yeah?

05:23.180 --> 05:25.933
- Pillow fight!
- Ow. You bastard.

05:42.203 --> 05:44.330
- Aah!
- Oh, my God. Sorry, Lois.

05:44.538 --> 05:48.668
Peter, what is our infant son
doing up on the roof?

05:48.877 --> 05:50.337
There's a raccoon up here.

05:50.545 --> 05:53.049
Yikes. Looks like I need a distraction.

05:53.257 --> 05:55.593
Ladies and gentlemen,
Mr. Conway Twitty.

08:43.457 --> 08:47.044
Terrific. Terrific.
So, Lois, you still pissed at me...

08:47.253 --> 08:49.923
...about Stewie being on the roof?
- Yes, Peter, I am.

08:50.090 --> 08:52.467
For crying out loud.
If Conway Twitty isn't enough...

08:52.676 --> 08:54.220
...to lighten you up,
what is it gonna take?

08:54.428 --> 08:56.389
A Minotaur with Sean Connery's head?

08:59.517 --> 09:01.478
Is this 31 Spooner S...?

09:01.687 --> 09:03.772
Get out of here.
Just get the hell out of here.

09:06.776 --> 09:09.445
Look, Lois, what do you say
we just bury the hatchet, huh?

09:09.612 --> 09:13.075
We'll stay in tonight, pop some popcorn,
and watch Jimmy Kimmel try.

09:13.284 --> 09:16.287
No, thank you, Peter.
And even if I wanted to, the TV's out.

09:16.453 --> 09:18.415
There must be something wrong
with the dish.

09:18.623 --> 09:22.670
It's all right, it's all right. I'll fix the dish.
Where's my screwdriver?

09:22.837 --> 09:24.797
Holy crap.

09:25.006 --> 09:27.550
You are not gonna believe
what I just found.

09:27.758 --> 09:29.011
A yellow piece of paper?

09:29.219 --> 09:32.472
A raffle ticket, Brian.
But not just any raffle ticket.

09:32.681 --> 09:35.977
I won this in 1989 from
a Honey Nut Cheerios sweepstakes...

09:36.185 --> 09:37.979
...and I totally forgot to cash it in.

09:38.146 --> 09:40.524
It's one free round of golf
with a famous celebrity.

09:40.774 --> 09:43.736
- Wow. Who's the celebrity?
- I'll give you a hint.

09:43.944 --> 09:46.948
<i>Famous football player.
Had a bit part in Roots.</i>

09:47.157 --> 09:49.534
<i>Couple of great scenes
in The Towering Inferno.</i>

09:49.743 --> 09:51.370
- Wait a minute.
- Chuck Connors?

09:51.579 --> 09:53.748
<i>He was a basketball player,
and he was in Roots.</i>

09:53.956 --> 09:56.543
<i>Yeah, he wasn't in
The Towering Inferno, you dumb beaver.</i>

09:56.752 --> 09:59.338
What? I didn't say nothing.

09:59.546 --> 10:01.840
- Dad, who is it?
- O.J. Simpson.

10:03.259 --> 10:06.846
- Who's that?
- O.J. Simpson on Spooner Street?

10:07.055 --> 10:10.059
Now, that's a story
I can sink my teeth into.

10:10.267 --> 10:12.061
Stick around.

10:17.776 --> 10:23.032
Peter, why in the world would you want
to play golf with O.J. Simpson?

10:23.240 --> 10:26.745
Why not, Lois? He's the Juice.
One of the greatest football players ever.

10:26.953 --> 10:29.539
Peter, he murdered two people.

10:29.748 --> 10:31.292
- What?
- He brutally killed...

10:31.459 --> 10:34.587
...his ex-wife Nicole Brown Simpson
and her friend Ron Goldman.

10:34.796 --> 10:36.840
- O.J. Simpson?
- Yes.

10:37.049 --> 10:40.552
- Was this in the news?
- Yes, Peter. It was all over the news.

10:40.761 --> 10:43.598
Wait. If he killed two people,
how come he's not in jail?

10:43.765 --> 10:46.351
- He was acquitted.
- Oh, there you go. Everything's fine.

10:46.559 --> 10:49.647
Well, Peter, it's generally believed
that the jury made a mistake.

10:49.814 --> 10:52.191
You're saying all those guys
in their powdery wigs...

10:52.399 --> 10:55.612
...and their pilgrim hats
and their big gross wives were wrong?

10:55.821 --> 10:59.575
Man, they'd have to be stupider than
you are when you fart yourself awake.

11:00.993 --> 11:03.371
Hello? What the...? What?
Who's there? What's going on?

11:04.330 --> 11:08.460
Whatever's happening here,
just knock it off.

11:12.882 --> 11:17.096
So I, Peter Griffin, will be playing
one free round of golf tomorrow...

11:17.263 --> 11:20.015
...with the one and only O.J. Simpson.

11:20.182 --> 11:24.104
What? Peter, you can't play golf
with O.J. Simpson. He's a murderer.

11:24.312 --> 11:27.148
Oh, you sound just like Lois.
No, no, Joe, I don't believe you.

11:27.357 --> 11:30.778
Oh, yeah? Well, say that after
a soul-searching walk around town...

11:30.987 --> 11:32.446
...to "Dust in the Wind. "

12:03.066 --> 12:06.820
Oh, my God, Joe, you're right.
O.J. Simpson is a murderer.

12:07.029 --> 12:09.532
What am I gonna do?
I'm playing golf with him tomorrow.

12:09.741 --> 12:13.787
Well, now, wait a minute, Peter. This
may be an unprecedented opportunity.

12:13.954 --> 12:16.248
Maybe you could wear a wire,
get O.J. To confess...

12:16.457 --> 12:18.835
...and we could tape the whole thing.

12:19.044 --> 12:22.922
Imagine it: Peter Griffin,
the guy who took down O.J.

12:23.131 --> 12:25.551
Marcia Clark sure couldn't do it,
that dumb beaver.

12:25.760 --> 12:30.724
Hey. I wasn't even there. I was building
a Canadian dam at the time.

12:30.932 --> 12:33.602
Did you know that beavers
affect their ecosystem...

12:33.769 --> 12:35.562
...more than any other animal?

12:35.771 --> 12:37.357
Except man.

12:37.565 --> 12:40.026
Ha-ha-ha. He was in our house earlier.

12:42.988 --> 12:44.031
Now, remember, Peter...

12:44.239 --> 12:46.825
...we're gonna be here in the van
if anything goes wrong.

12:47.034 --> 12:49.537
Just try to get O.J. Talking
about the murders.

12:49.746 --> 12:52.916
Do you think he'd be offended
if I asked him to sign this basketball?

12:53.125 --> 12:55.419
- Yeah, I think he'd be very offended.
- Oh.

12:57.463 --> 12:58.757
All right, Joe. Can you hear me?

12:58.965 --> 13:00.842
<i>Loud and clear, Peter.</i>

13:04.514 --> 13:08.267
Oh, man, I don't think I can do this.
Joe, say something to relax me.

13:27.541 --> 13:29.376
<i>That's right, Peter.</i>

13:32.337 --> 13:33.464
Thanks. I feel better.

13:34.882 --> 13:37.552
- Are you Peter Griffin?
- That's my name. Don't put a knife in it.

13:37.718 --> 13:40.264
Nice to meet you.
Come on, let's tee off.

13:42.224 --> 13:45.520
Damn it. Will you look at these
golf shoes? They're all scuffed up.

13:45.728 --> 13:49.190
My wife was supposed to polish them,
but, clearly, she forgot.

13:49.399 --> 13:53.445
Man, sometimes I just feel like
I could just stab her repeatedly. Heh.

13:53.612 --> 13:56.700
White women, huh? Jewish waiters too.

13:56.908 --> 13:59.911
I got this Jewish waiter one time.
He was awful. Didn't tip him.

14:00.120 --> 14:02.081
You ever do anything bad
to a Jewish waiter?

14:02.290 --> 14:05.126
What's that, Peter? I'm sorry.
I was focusing on my drive.

14:05.293 --> 14:08.046
You're doing great, Peter.
Just don't let him intimidate you.

14:08.255 --> 14:11.008
Guys, guys, someone's getting frogged
in the clubhouse.

14:11.216 --> 14:13.178
- Quagmire.
- She sounds fat.

14:14.637 --> 14:16.598
You know what I like
to do sometimes, Juice?

14:16.806 --> 14:19.143
I like to just confess things
I've done to people.

14:19.351 --> 14:23.022
You know? Just clear my conscience.
Makes me feel a whole lot better.

14:23.230 --> 14:25.734
- Anything you'd like to confess?
- No, not really.

14:25.942 --> 14:29.571
<i>Peter, we're not really hearing him
very well. Can you get closer?</i>

14:31.198 --> 14:34.660
Are you sure, O. J? Are you sure
you wouldn't like to confess...

14:34.869 --> 14:37.331
...to the murders of Nicole
Brown Simpson and Ron Goldman?

14:37.539 --> 14:38.540
What?

14:39.958 --> 14:41.210
What the hell is that?

14:41.419 --> 14:43.630
You're wearing a wire.

14:44.380 --> 14:45.840
I am so murdered.

14:46.049 --> 14:48.802
Peter, I'm hurt.
How could you deceive me like this?

14:49.011 --> 14:52.348
- Oh, God, O.J., please don't kill me.
- Wait a minute.

14:52.557 --> 14:55.769
Is this about that whole business
back in 1994?

14:55.977 --> 14:57.687
- Well, yeah.
- Darn it.

14:57.896 --> 15:00.358
That's been chasing me for 13 years.

15:00.566 --> 15:03.569
And here I was looking forward
to a nice day of golf...

15:03.778 --> 15:06.323
...away from all those people
who have demonized me...

15:06.531 --> 15:08.784
...and made me out to be
some kind of bogeyman...

15:08.992 --> 15:12.080
...even though I was found innocent
by a jury of my peers.

15:12.288 --> 15:13.748
But what about the civil trial?

15:13.956 --> 15:16.543
Believe me, Peter,
there was nothing civil about it.

15:16.752 --> 15:19.797
Ha-ha-ha.
Well, that makes up for one murder.

15:20.005 --> 15:23.134
The only thing I'm guilty of
is a few bad movies.

15:23.343 --> 15:26.346
And that makes up for the other murder.
I am sold.

15:26.554 --> 15:30.685
- You are so witty and charming.
- That's nice of you to say, Peter.

15:30.893 --> 15:33.563
It's been so long since I've had a friend.

15:36.983 --> 15:38.611
You poor fella.

15:38.820 --> 15:41.072
Gosh, there's no way
you could've killed anybody.

15:41.280 --> 15:42.824
Not with those sad eyes.

15:42.990 --> 15:45.828
I'm gonna make sure
everything's gonna be all right.

15:46.328 --> 15:48.997
Hey, everybody.
Look who I brought home.

15:49.206 --> 15:51.167
Ten thousand rushing yards,
six Pro Bowls...

15:51.376 --> 15:54.129
...two arrests and no convictions,
Orenthal James Simpson.

15:54.295 --> 15:55.297
Hi, Griffins.

15:55.506 --> 15:56.549
- Oh, my God.
- What the...?

15:56.757 --> 15:58.134
I just think you're terrific.

15:58.342 --> 16:00.302
O.J. Simpson?

16:00.511 --> 16:05.934
I may be a dumb beaver,
but I'm smart enough to get out of here.

16:11.774 --> 16:15.821
- O.J., this is my family. Family, O.J.
- It's nice to meet you all.

16:16.029 --> 16:17.991
Hey, Peter,
you mind if I use your restroom?

16:18.199 --> 16:20.076
No. It's upstairs and to the left.

16:20.285 --> 16:23.747
Peter, are you out of your mind
bringing O.J. Simpson into our home?

16:23.956 --> 16:27.042
Look, don't make that face at me, Lois.
O.J. Is innocent, all right?

16:27.251 --> 16:28.252
- Innocent?
- Yes.

16:28.461 --> 16:31.381
The most perfect justice system
in the world found him innocent.

16:31.548 --> 16:33.341
- But we know he did it.
- You were there?

16:33.550 --> 16:36.137
I didn't realize that.
You didn't do anything to stop it?

16:36.345 --> 16:37.346
Accessory to murder.

16:37.555 --> 16:39.265
Why are you so quick
to defend this guy?

16:39.474 --> 16:41.727
Because he was a childhood hero, Brian.

16:41.935 --> 16:45.189
Yes, he had a few marital problems,
but I used to look up to him.

16:45.397 --> 16:48.067
That's it, isn't it?
You idolized O.J. Simpson as a boy...

16:48.234 --> 16:51.154
...and you can't accept
that he's not who you thought he was.

16:51.362 --> 16:54.533
Enough with the yappity-yap.
O.J. Is gonna stay with us in Quahog...

16:54.742 --> 16:57.161
...until I can help him
get his life back on track.

17:01.499 --> 17:02.500
Hi, Lois.

17:03.920 --> 17:07.632
- Oh. Hello, O.J.
- Anything I can do to help make dinner?

17:07.840 --> 17:10.510
Um... Sure. You can take the lasagna
out of the oven.

17:10.677 --> 17:11.929
You got it.

17:14.849 --> 17:20.814
Oh, wouldn't you know it? It won't fit.
Well, it's all right. How hot can it be?

17:21.065 --> 17:23.943
Ah, ooh, ooh, ow, ow, ow!

17:24.151 --> 17:25.861
Oh, Lois, I'm so sorry.

17:26.028 --> 17:28.949
It's all right, O.J.
Let me get something to clean that up.

17:29.157 --> 17:30.867
- Ooh!
- Aah!

17:31.034 --> 17:33.496
- Oh, my God! Oh, my God!
- Brian, what's the matter?

17:33.704 --> 17:37.918
- Oh. You're alive.
- Yeah, we just had a little pasta spill.

17:38.085 --> 17:40.170
Oh, thank God. Oh.

17:40.379 --> 17:42.005
It's okay, Brian.

17:42.214 --> 17:44.634
It's not the first accident
we've had in this house.

17:45.176 --> 17:46.886
Okay, one, two...

17:47.053 --> 17:49.556
Hang on. Hang on, Brian.
Stop the wheel. Stop the wheel.

17:49.765 --> 17:50.766
I BM'd.

17:50.975 --> 17:53.143
Hey, Juice.
Is it all right if I call you Juice?

17:53.352 --> 17:55.730
Great. I was wondering
if you could give me advice...

17:55.939 --> 17:58.191
...on how to murder a woman
and get away with it.

17:58.400 --> 18:01.237
Cool. Look at that. Hey, Chris, go long.

18:04.573 --> 18:08.286
- Touchdown!
Good grief.

18:09.121 --> 18:10.247
What are you doing, O. J?

18:10.455 --> 18:13.710
Well, I got no money left
to pay off my civil-suit debt...

18:13.918 --> 18:16.921
...so I'm making a god's eye
to send to Fred Goldman.

18:17.840 --> 18:19.883
It's kind of nice, right?
Better than nothing.

18:20.092 --> 18:23.763
He's got money to buy tongue depressors
and yarn, but not enough to pay us back?

18:23.972 --> 18:26.391
You know how much mustache cream
that could've bought?

18:26.599 --> 18:29.270
I don't like the mustache, Fred.
Nobody likes the mustache.

18:29.478 --> 18:32.898
- That's why we lost the trial.
- That's not true.

18:39.906 --> 18:42.118
<i>- Good evening. I'm Tom Tucker.
- I'm Diane Simmons.</i>

18:42.326 --> 18:45.580
<i>Our top story: Quahog, Rhode Island,
known for quaint neighborhoods...</i>

18:45.788 --> 18:50.002
<i>...white, sandy beaches,
and harboring bloodthirsty murderers?</i>

18:50.210 --> 18:51.211
<i>That's right, Tom.</i>

18:51.420 --> 18:54.090
<i>Former murderer O.J. Simpson
has moved to Quahog.</i>

18:54.299 --> 18:57.595
<i>We don't have footage of the murder,
but we can show you what happened...</i>

18:57.803 --> 19:00.639
<i>...thanks to this re-enactment
by the Quahog Opera Company.</i>

19:03.769 --> 19:06.271
<i>I love you, Nicole</i>

19:06.480 --> 19:09.734
<i>But I must confess</i>

19:09.942 --> 19:12.487
<i>To some trepidation</i>

19:12.695 --> 19:16.116
<i>For I am a lonely waiter</i>

19:16.325 --> 19:22.123
<i>Who loves a lass above his station</i>

19:22.791 --> 19:24.709
<i>But soft, Ron</i>

19:24.918 --> 19:27.838
<i>My husband draws near</i>

19:28.005 --> 19:29.381
<i>Nicole</i>

19:29.548 --> 19:35.847
<i>I'm back from filming
The third Naked Gun movie</i>

19:37.850 --> 19:39.644
<i>Oh, horror</i>

19:39.852 --> 19:41.854
<i>You have betrayed me</i>

19:42.063 --> 19:46.193
<i>Al Cowling said it would be so</i>

19:46.401 --> 19:48.111
<i>Kato</i>

19:48.320 --> 19:55.287
<i>I didn't see a thing</i>

19:57.873 --> 20:01.920
Well, it looks like this is one more town
the media's run me out of.

20:02.128 --> 20:05.340
Now, wait a second. You can't let them
tell you how to live your life.

20:05.549 --> 20:07.093
You've been running for too long.

20:07.260 --> 20:10.096
I say you let people get to know you
the way I have.

20:10.263 --> 20:12.766
- You really think that's possible?
- Of course it is.

20:12.975 --> 20:15.352
We'll throw a big party
and invite everybody in town.

20:15.561 --> 20:17.522
And I promise they'll accept you.

20:20.733 --> 20:24.446
Peter, I really appreciate this,
but are you sure people are ready?

20:24.655 --> 20:28.033
Absolutely. This party will give you
a chance to get to know everybody...

20:28.242 --> 20:31.079
...and give them a chance
to get to know the real O.J. Simpson.

20:31.288 --> 20:33.748
Peter, do you really expect
anyone to show up?

20:33.957 --> 20:36.544
Sure, I do.
Look, here comes a bunch of people.

20:41.049 --> 20:42.843
Wow, what a turnout.

20:43.051 --> 20:45.555
Peter, that's not a group
of enthusiastic party guests.

20:45.763 --> 20:46.889
That's an angry mob.

20:49.100 --> 20:51.228
We don't want you in our town,
Simpson.

20:51.437 --> 20:55.107
- We don't love you like we did in 1993.
- D'oh!

20:55.316 --> 20:58.820
And as for you, O.J.,
we don't want you here either.

21:02.783 --> 21:04.160
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa.

21:04.368 --> 21:07.496
Anyone who wants a piece of O.J.
Has to get by me.

21:07.705 --> 21:11.626
No, Peter. This is my fight,
and I'll be the one to fight it.

21:12.127 --> 21:14.213
Look at you all. Look what you're doing.

21:14.422 --> 21:17.258
Why, you're no better
than what you've made me out to be.

21:17.467 --> 21:19.594
Sure, I've made some mistakes
in my life.

21:19.803 --> 21:21.930
I forget to take the trash out some days.

21:22.139 --> 21:24.808
I've left the toothpaste cap
on the bathroom counter.

21:24.975 --> 21:27.896
I've taped football games
without the express written consent...

21:28.063 --> 21:29.856
...of the National Football League.

21:30.065 --> 21:33.611
I guess what I'm saying is,
I'm not perfect.

21:33.819 --> 21:36.572
The only difference is
I have the courage to admit it.

21:36.782 --> 21:39.159
Does anyone else have the courage?

21:39.367 --> 21:42.413
If so, why don't you just
come on up here and join me?

21:42.622 --> 21:45.500
He's right. I'm not perfect.

21:47.502 --> 21:50.005
I suppose I'm not either.

21:52.007 --> 21:56.304
- Yeah, I guess none of us are perfect.
- Boy, do I feel like a jerk.

21:56.513 --> 22:00.976
- Me too.
- I think we owe you an apology, O.J.

22:03.521 --> 22:05.816
You see? None of us are perfect.

22:19.373 --> 22:20.833
Oh, I guess he did do it.

22:20.834 --> 24:21.834
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru